    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d296">

                <pb facs="0504" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1933v01/pg402"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Four Power Pact/21: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Garrett</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-04-03T18:00:00+01:00">April 3, 1933—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 3—2:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>20. My 18, March 22, 10 a.m.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d296-f1"/> The British
                    Ambassador presented to the chief of the Italian Government this afternoon a
                    revised text of the proposed four power pact. He tells me that it differs from
                    the second text in two points, namely: <list>
                        <label>(1)</label>
                        <item>Any reference to a possible failure of the Disarmament Conference is
                            omitted.</item>
                        <pb facs="0505" n="403" xml:id="pg403"/>
                        <label>(2)</label>
                        <item>Any power will be admitted at its request as an equal in any
                            discussions that may concern it.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>This third text has also been handed by Lord Tyrrell<anchor n="28"
                        xml:id="d296-f2"/> to the French Government and Sir Ronald Graham believes
                    will be transmitted to Berlin through the Italian Ambassador there. Mussolini
                    agreed to it in principle.</p>
                <p>Repeated to the American Embassy, Paris, for Norman Davis.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Garrett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
